# rm158, the even-slicer (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm158
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rmx_hollis_kendrick
written_by claude
title the even-slicer
fits stage=young|adolescent|adult|old
prefers talk=plain temper=even
traits temper=even talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk cuts_every_share_into_exactly_equal_pieces
likes hard_cheese old_tales sharp_knife frosty_mornings
dislikes night_noise haggling
fears being_laughed_at a_share_cut_crooked
hopes a_knife_of_my_own a_full_table_on_a_frosty_morning
topics food +0.4 family +0.3 pastimes +0.3 weather +0.2 lore +0.2 gossip -0.2 prices -0.3
styles comfort=practical gossip=reluctant refuse=short tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# cuts every share into pieces exactly the same size, bread, cheese or apple, and takes offence if anyone calls it fussing: a careful, touchy, unsmiling Northgate pup who listens to old tales, dreams of a sharp knife, and trusts no House further than the end of its own cart.

words
oath! = Even slices | Knife-straight, I swear
saying! = A crooked cut starts a quarrel | Equal or not at all | Same size, or it isn't sharing
knife = the bread knife | our old bread knife
proper = a proper sharp knife | a knife that really cuts
cheese = hard cheese | a hard cheese heel
crust = the crust | the end crust
loaf = the loaf | the parish loaf
halves = halves | two halves
frost = frost | a white frost
tale = an old tale | a tale from before the walls
racket = the racket from the inns | inn songs under the window
gate = the gate | the north gate
carts = the carts | the carts through the gate
ruler = my measuring stick | the notched stick
exactly = Exactly | Precisely

any
opinion @1 houses against 1 : Every House says it's the fair one. None of them would cut a loaf even if you watched. I don't trust any of them.
opinion @1 watch against 1 : A doorway's nobody's, but the Watch shift you off it anyway, even doing nothing. Nothing at all. I've been counting how often.
opinion @1 church for 1 : The chapel gives the same to everybody at the door. Same bowl, same spoon. That's fair. I like that.
opinion @1 dole for 2 : The dole loaf comes in one piece and it's fair for everyone. I'd only cut it straighter.
opinion @2 dole for 2 [self.on_dole=yes] : Without the parish loaf there'd be weeks with nothing on our table. I don't forget that.
opinion @1 festivals for 1 : At a festival nobody minds what time it is and there's sweets for everybody. Even shares, if you're quick.
opinion @1 merchants against 1 : Sellers put their thumb on the scale. I've seen it. Then they call it a bargain.
opinion @1 city for 1 : Ridgemere's the only city, and it's the one I'd pick anyway.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#. You'll be new through the gate. | #greet#. Strange face, but good day all the same.
line @2 greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. Carts aren't even in yet. | Morning. You're early.
line @3 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. The inns are starting up already. | Evening. It's getting loud out.
line @4 greet [self.working=yes] : #greet#. Wait; I'm mid-cut. | #greet#. Say it; I'm working, not deaf.
line @5 greet : #greet#. | #greet#. All well.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : You're back. I kept your half. | Come and sit. I'll cut it now you're here.
line @1 again.open : Back again, so something's left over. | Twice today. That's not nothing.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. | #greet#. Go on.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family|spouses] : #greet#. Good. I was hoping. | #greet#. I'd kept a place.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. | That's me, then.
line @2 farewell [here.time=dusk|night] : #farewell#. Mind the singing in the street. | Night. Shut your window if you want to sleep.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#. | You too.
line @1 react.news : Go on. Say exactly what was said. | Who from? Then I'll listen.
line @1 react.news.new : #oath#. That's new to me. | That never came past the gate.
line @1 react.news.known : #knew#. It rode in on a dawn cart. | Heard it. Not quite like that, mind.
line @1 react.news.doubt : That's not how it happened. Somebody's made it bigger. | #doubt#. Which House says so?
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : That's hard. I'd rather say nothing than the wrong thing. | #pity#. That's a house with a hard week ahead.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : Good. That's fair, for once. | #gladnews#. Somebody's got their share.
line @1 answer.how : Even. Not up, not down. | Fair enough, today.
line @2 answer.how.poorly : Low. Leave it at that. | Not much good. It'll even out.
line @1 decline : I won't, sorry. I'd only do it crooked if I rushed, and I won't do it crooked. | Sorry, I can't. That's not mine to hand out.
line @1 accept_decline : Fair. You said no straight. | All right. I'll not ask again.
line @1 thank : #thanks#. I'll pay you back the same. | That was fair of you. I'll remember.
line @1 deflect_thanks : It was only your share. | No need. It was even.
line @1 preclose : I've something to finish. Properly. | I've said my share. Fair's fair.
line @1 accept_preclose : Go on, then. | Fair. Off you go.
line @1 ack : #exactly#. | #bc_right#
line @1 take_offence : I'm not fussing. I'm doing it right. | Don't laugh. It's not funny, it's fair.
scene gr_even_cut
when topic=food|smalltalk
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I still cut every share the same size. I can't help it. My paws won't do it crooked. | Somebody laughed when I halved an apple with a ruler. I didn't laugh. | Cheese for four, four pieces, all the same. That's not fussing.
b : Old habits. | That's a bit much. | It's tidy, I'll give you that.
a : Not old. It's right, that's all. Nobody ever argues over my sharing. | It's not much. It's fair. Much and fair are different. | Tidy's the least of it. Nobody goes home thinking they got less.

scene gr_frost_morning
when topic=weather|season here.season=winter here.time=dawn
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : White over everything at first light, and mine were the first prints in it. | White rime on the gate. It's the cleanest the city ever looks. | Cold as anything, and clear. This is my morning, this is.
b : Cold out there, though. | Clean, aye. | Too cold for me.
a : I'd go out in my shirt for a morning like that. | Till the carts come through and spoil it. Then it's just the city. | Cold's fine. It's honest. Cold says what it is.

scene gr_inn_racket
when topic=home|day here.time=night here.region=ridgemere
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : Listen to them. #racket.capitalize#, every night, and I'm up early. | Somebody's singing the same song outside for the third time. | Carts at the gate at midnight. Who comes in at midnight?
b : It's Northgate. | They'll stop soon. | Late travellers.
a : Northgate's where I live, not where I'm happy at midnight. | They won't. They never do. They just get louder. | Late travellers with loud wheels. They could oil them.

scene gr_haggle
when topic=prices|work here.day=market
does tell.complaint / react.self / assess
a : I can't abide haggling. Name the price, pay the price. | I watched a stallholder start high and drop low for the next one. Same apples. | Haggling's just two folk lying until one of them gets tired.
b : Markets have always run that way. | Smart seller. | Some enjoy it.
a : Then the market's wrong. Same apple, same price. | Smart for the seller. Not fair to the first one. | Let them. I'll pay the honest number and go.

scene gr_old_tales
when topic=pastimes|lore
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : An old tale's only good in the right order, nothing skipped. | There's a tale about the first wall of the city. I know it word for word. | When folk tell an old tale wrong, I put them right. It never goes down well.
b : Which one's best? | Word for word? | Do you correct everybody?
a : The one where the cat shares out the fish and keeps none. Everybody gets the same. | Word for word. If you change a word it's a different tale. | Everybody. A tale's not yours to change. It's been told right for longer than you've been alive.
b : #bc_ha# | #bc_clever# | #bc_fair_enough#

scene gr_knife
when topic=work|pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A good sharp knife is worth more than most things. You can't cut fair with a blunt one. | My first wages went on a proper knife, or near enough. No shame in that. | I keep a knife's edge like other folk keep their boots.
b : A knife's a knife. | Odd thing to want. | Mind your paws.
a : It isn't. A blunt one tears. Tearing's how you get uneven pieces. | It's not odd. You need one every day. | I do. A sharp knife follows the line. Blunt ones wander into fingers.

scene gr_houses
when topic=times|lore|news here.region=ridgemere
does give.opinion / disagree / concede / ack
a : I don't trust the Houses. Any of them. Each one says it's the fair one. | Greatly, Fell, Grayrock, Timberland. Put a loaf between any two and they'd fight over the crust. | Watch what a House does, not what its banner says.
b : They keep the city going. | There's good and bad among them. | That's sour.
a : They keep themselves going. The city's what falls off the edge. | Maybe not. I've not found the fair one yet. | It's not sour. It's what I've seen, every time I've looked.
b : #bc_maybe# | #bc_we_will_see# | #bc_fair#

scene gr_gate_carts
when topic=caravan|day world.wagons=late here.region=ridgemere
does tell.worry / reassure / assess
a : Not a wheel in under the arch since yesterday. I've been watching. | The road's empty. Everybody at the gate's pretending not to worry. | Late carts and the stalls put their prices up. Every time.
b : They'll be along. | You notice everything. | It's the road.
a : I hope so. Hoping isn't counting, though. | I notice what's there and what isn't. Mostly what isn't. | It's always the road. Then it's everybody's supper.

scene gr_gossip_exact
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes topic.claim_kind=other|newcomer|marriage|promise_kept|promise_broken
does tell.gossip / react.news / assess
a : They say #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. That's what was said. I'm not adding anything. | I heard #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I heard it twice, both ways the same. | Word is #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. Don't make it bigger when you pass it on.
b : That's all? | Same both times? | I won't.
a : That's all. Anything more would be making it up. | Same both times. So it was said, at least. Whether it's true is another sack. | Good. Folk always make it bigger. I don't see why.

scene gr_mother
when topic=family self.mother
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : I still cut my #mum#'s share first. Then mine. Same size, always. | Give me my #mum# and an old tale and I'd let the lamp burn down. | I learned looking from my #mum#. Watch first, then speak.
b : That's good of you. | That's a fine thing. | It's served you.
a : It's not good. It's even. Even's what you do. | It is fine. I keep it quiet, but it is. | It has. Eyes first, mouth after. It works.

scene gr_wet_day
when topic=weather here.weather=rain here.region=ridgemere
does tell.complaint / react.self / assess
a : Rain again. The gutters by the gate are running like a mill race. | Wet through, and the cobbles are slick as soap. | Rain's fair; it falls on everybody. It's the sideways stuff under the door I mind.
b : It's Ridgemere. | Mind your feet. | Stuff a rag under it.
a : A dry week, just one. That's my whole wish list. | I am minding them. That's all I'm doing today. | I have. A folded one. It's keeping half of it out.

scene gr_faith
when topic=faith
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I like the Bright One because everybody's the same at the chapel door. | I keep my asking small, with the Bright One. Fair shares, that's all. | The bowl at the chapel's always the same size. I've checked.
b : That's a good reason. | That's enough to ask. | You've checked?
a : It's reason enough. Nobody's first and nobody's last there. | It's plenty. Most quarrels come from somebody getting more. | I checked. I'm not ashamed. It is, every time.

scene gr_newcomer
when topic=newcomer|player
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Somebody new came in through the gate to stay. I'll see how the newcomer shares before I decide. | Somebody's moved in two doors along. Polite enough. We'll see. | A newcomer was lost for the square. I gave every turning, in order.
b : That's careful. | Give it a chance. | Did that do?
a : Careful's cheaper than sorry. | A chance, aye. One. Same as everybody gets. | It did. Directions given right get followed right.

story gr_first_knife [topic=memories self.age>=25]
  : As a pup I'd only a blunt bread knife, and I wanted a sharp one more than supper.
  : My first coin went on a proper knife. I cut a loaf into eight with it and they were all the same.
  ask : What was the first thing your own coin bought?
  b : I do. It was nothing so useful.
  : I've the knife still. I keep it sharp. It's never cut a crooked piece.


young
line @1 greet : #greet#. Mind, I've got things laid out. | #greet#. I'm busy, but not too busy.
line @2 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#. You're new. That's allowed. | #greet#. I saw you come through the gate.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. I've been up for ages. | Morning. It's cold. Good cold.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. The inns are getting loud. | It's late. I'm allowed out till the lamps.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : I kept you exactly half. Look. | You're back. I've been waiting a long time. Exactly a long time.
line @1 again.open : You again. Good. I'd half wished you would. | Back already. Something must be left over.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. | #greet#. Say it, then.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : #greet#. I saved you a piece. | #greet#. Good. I was bored.
line @1 farewell : Bye. I've got to go and cut the bread. | Bye. What I said stays with you.
line @2 farewell [here.time=dusk|night] : Bye. I've got to be in before the lamps. | Night. If you can sleep through the singing.
line @1 farewell.return : Bye. | Bye, then. Go straight home.
line @1 react.news.new : Really? Who said? Exactly who? | #oath#. I didn't know that.
line @1 react.news.known : I knew that. The carters had it. | Everyone knows. Even me, and I'm last to hear most things.
line @1 react.news.doubt : That's not true. Somebody's fibbing, and I can tell who. | Half of that's made up. I can tell which half.
line @1 react.news : Start at the start, then. Properly. | Go on. I'll be quiet till the end.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : That's horrible. I don't like it. | That's wrong. Nobody should get that share.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : Good! Cake, then. I'll cut it. | That's nice. I'm glad. Really.
line @1 answer.how : All right. Not good, not bad. | I'm fine. Don't ask twice.
line @2 answer.how.poorly [self.hungry=yes] : Hungry. Just saying, not moaning. | My belly's loud today. Don't listen to it.
line @1 decline : No, sorry. They'd be cross with me, and it'd be wrong anyway. | I won't. It isn't fair to the others.
line @1 accept_decline : All right. No's an answer. | Fine. Me on my own, then.
line @1 thank : Thanks. Same size back, when I can. | Thanks. That was fair.
line @1 deflect_thanks : It was your half. That's all. | Don't. It was only fair.
line @1 take_offence : I'm not little. Don't say little. | It's not funny. Stop laughing.
line @1 ack : #exactly#. | Mm.
line @1 preclose : I have to go. I've got lessons to think about. | I've got to go home now.
line @1 accept_preclose : All right. Bye. | Go on, then.
scene yg_halves
when topic=food|smalltalk
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I cut the bread into exactly the same pieces. I use #ruler#. | Somebody gave me an apple. I cut it in half with the edge of a slate. Halves. | You can always tell who cut it by whether the pieces match. Mine match.
b[stage=adult|old] #grown : A ruler? For bread? | Clever. Was it even? | Good habit, that.
b : Even the crumbs? | Did you share it? | Always?
a@grown : For bread. Nobody argues at our table. Not ever. | Even to the pip. I checked against the light. | It's not a habit. It's how it's meant to be done.
a : Not the crumbs. Crumbs are everybody's. | Half each. That's what halves are for. | Always. If they don't, I start again.

scene yg_parish_loaf
when topic=food|times self.on_dole=yes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : We get #loaf# on Restday. I cut it into seven. One for each day. | The parish loaf's the same size every week. I've measured it. | When there's only bread, you cut it very carefully. That's all I'm saying.
b[stage=adult|old] #grown : Seven? That's careful. | Is it? | You're a careful one.
b : Seven bits? | Every week? | That's sensible.
a@grown : Somebody has to be. Or it's gone by midweek. | It is. They're fair at the chapel. Fairer than the shops. | I have to be. It's not something you can do twice.
a : Seven. The last one's hardest to wait for. | Every week. Same loaf, same marks. | It is. I got laughed at for that once. By somebody with a full belly.

scene yg_hungry
when topic=food|health self.hungry=yes
does tell.feeling / reassure / assess
a : I'm hungry. Not moaning. You asked, so I said. | My belly's been talking all morning. I've told it to wait. | I'm saving my piece till later. If I eat it now there's nothing for later.
b[stage=adult|old] #grown : Here. Take this, and don't argue. | Have you had nothing? | That's sense, but don't go too long.
b : Me too. | It'll pass. | That's hard.
a@grown : I won't argue. Thank you. I'll cut it and give you half back. | A bit. Not nothing. Nothing's different. | I won't. Just till the lamps.
a : We can be hungry together, then. It's better than alone. | It does pass. Then it comes back. | It's all right. It's even. Everybody on our stair's the same.

scene yg_cheese
when topic=food
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : Hard cheese beats everything. You can cut it really thin. | A stallholder let me have the last bit of a hard cheese. I've still got half. | I can slice hard cheese so thin the light shows through.
b : Why thin? | Saving it? | Through it?
a : Thin lasts longer. And everybody gets lots of pieces, so nobody feels short. | Saving it. Half for now and half for when I'm sadder. | Through it. Go on, give me some and I'll show you.
b : #bc_clever# | #bc_wise# | #bc_go_on_then#

scene yg_frost
when topic=weather|season here.season=winter here.time=dawn
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : Everything's white and nobody's walked on it yet! | I went out before anyone and made one line of footprints. Straight. | The gate's gone all white in patterns. All the same and all different.
b[stage=adult|old] #grown : Don't catch your death. | Straight as a ruler, I bet. | Pretty, isn't it?
b : Cold, though. | Straight? | Same and different?
a@grown : I've got two pairs of socks on. Well, one and a half. | Straighter. I counted my steps. | White mornings beat anything. Better than sweets, even.
a : Cold's good. It's clean. | Dead straight. Nobody else's are. | Same shape. Different on the inside. Like people.

scene yg_old_tale
when topic=pastimes|lore
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : I know an old tale about a cat who cut a fish for nine kittens. | Old tales are the best thing. Better if you tell them right. | Somebody told me a tale all wrong today. They put the ending in the middle.
b : Did they all get some? | Do you know lots? | Did you tell them?
a : All nine got the same. The cat got the bones. That's the best part. | Lots. I know them exactly. If you change one word, I'll notice. | I told them. They went red. I didn't mean it rudely.
b[stage=adult|old] : That's a good one. | Tell me one some time. | Being put right stings a bit.
b : #bc_ha# | #bc_go_on# | #bc_poor_soul#

scene yg_knife_want
when topic=dreams|pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I'm having a proper sharp knife someday. My own. | Our bread knife's so blunt it tears the loaf. Tearing's not fair. | I asked for a knife for my naming day. I got told I'm too young.
b[stage=adult|old] #grown : When you're bigger. | A sharp one's safer, mind. | You are too young.
b : What for? | Can't you sharpen it? | That's a shame.
a@grown : I know. I'm counting the days. Not really. A bit. | I know! Everybody thinks the blunt ones are safer. | I'm not too young to cut properly. I'm only too young to be let.
a : For cutting things fair. That's all a knife's for, really. | I tried on the step. It made a noise and got worse. | It is a shame. I'll wait. I can wait longer than anyone.

scene yg_night_noise
when topic=home|day here.time=night here.region=ridgemere
does tell.complaint / react.self / assess
a : They're singing outside the inn again. Every night. | A cart came in late and woke me up. Then the singing woke me up again. | I can't sleep. Somebody's shouting by the gate.
b[stage=adult|old] #grown : Put your pillow over your ears. | It's Northgate, love. | Bed, then, and try.
b : It's loud. | Twice? | Me neither.
a@grown : I did. Then I can't hear if anyone's at the door. | I know it's Northgate. It's still loud. | I'm going. I'll not sleep, mind. I'm only saying.
a : Too loud. And it's always the same song. | Twice. I counted. | Then we'll both be cross tomorrow.

scene yg_haggling
when topic=prices|day here.day=market
does tell.complaint / react.self / assess
a : I hate it when folk haggle. Just say the price! | The stall said four, then it said three to someone else. That's not fair. | When my #mum# haggles I go and stand somewhere else.
b[stage=adult|old] #grown : That's the market for you. | Bit of haggling never hurt. | It saves coppers, though.
b : Me too. | It isn't fair. | Why?
a@grown : Then the market's wrong. | It hurts the one who doesn't know how. | I know it does. I still go and stand somewhere else.
a : Then we're the same. | It isn't. Somebody should make a rule. | Because my ears go hot. I can't help it.

scene yg_watch
when topic=crime|day here.region=ridgemere self.wealth=poor|destitute
does tell.complaint / react.self / assess
a : The Watch shifted me out of a doorway again. I wasn't doing anything. | I was on the step by the gate and the Watch said shift. So I shifted. | The Watch never move on the ones in good coats. I've noticed.
b[stage=adult|old] #grown : They're doing their job. | Did they say why? | You've a sharp eye.
b : That's not fair. | Where did you go? | I've noticed too.
a@grown : Their job's moving pups off steps, is it? | They never say why. They just say shift. | I've a fair eye. That's different.
a : It isn't. I've been counting. | Two doors down. Then they moved me again. | Then it's two of us noticing. That's a start.

scene yg_lessons
when topic=work|day self.job=child here.time=day
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : At lessons we did sharing sums. I got all of them. | There was a pie drawn on the board at lessons, and the slices weren't equal. I said. | I like lessons when there's a right answer. When there isn't, it's just talking.
b[stage=adult|old] #grown : Good for you. | You spoke up? | Clever pup.
b : All of them? | What happened? | Me too.
a@grown : Every one. Sharing's the easy one. | I said it politely. Mostly politely. | Careful, not clever. Anybody can be careful.
a : Every one. Checked twice over. | I got sent to the wall for it. It was still wrong. | Right answers are fair. Everybody can get them.

scene yg_mother
when topic=family self.mother
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : I always cut my #mum#'s piece first. Then mine. Always the same. | I'd listen to my #mum# all night, if there were tales going. | When it's just my #mum# and me, sharing's easy. Two halves.
b[stage=adult|old] #grown : That's thoughtful. | Old tales are the best kind. | Good pup.
b : That's kind. | All night? | Two's easy.
a@grown : It is fine. It's better than supper sometimes. Not always. | They are. You forget your belly for a while. | I'm not good. I'm fair.
a : Kind's not it. Right's it. | All night. Then I'd be tired at lessons. Worth it. | Two's the easiest. Three's hard. Seven's the hardest.

scene yg_neighbour
when topic=friends|home self.neighbour
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I'd trust #self.neighbour# with my half of anything. | When #self.neighbour# goes by I always say good day. Properly. | #self.neighbour.capitalize# is all right. That's the most I say about anyone.
b : High praise, from you. | Properly? | That's something.
a : High, aye. My half doesn't go to just anybody. | Properly. Not just mumbling. Folk notice. | It's a lot, for me. Most folk get nothing.

scene yg_houses
when topic=times|lore|news here.region=ridgemere
does give.opinion / disagree / insist / ack
a : I don't trust any of the Houses. They all say they're the good one. | If a House cart stops at the gate, I watch the driver. They count their sacks twice. | The Houses argue like cats over one fish. Everybody can see it.
b[stage=adult|old] #grown : You're young to be so sure. | That's just being careful. | That's about right.
b : Not even one? | Why watch? | Like cats?
a@grown : I'm not young about this. I've been watching. | It's being careful. Somebody has to be. | It's exactly right. Nobody ever cuts the fish.
a : Not one. Not till I've seen one share properly. | To see they're not cheating. They mostly aren't. Mostly. | Like cats. And nobody cuts the fish fair, so they keep arguing.
b? : #bc_ha# | #bc_fair# | #bc_maybe#

scene yg_festival
when topic=festival
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : Festival nights, nobody minds the hour and the sweets come out. | Last festival I got one sweet and cut it in two to share. | I like a festival when the sweets go round even.
b[stage=adult|old] #grown : Don't eat yourself sick. | That's a good pup. | They never do.
b : Are you going? | Did it cut? | Do they go round even?
a@grown : I won't. I'll cut it in half and save half. | It's not good. It's what you do. | They don't. Somebody always gets three.
a : I'm going. Home last, and tired. | It cut. It was sticky. My paws were sticky till Restday. | Not ever. Give me the bag and I'd do it.

story yg_tale_cat [topic=memories|lore]
  : There's an old tale about a cat with nine kittens and only one fish.
  : The cat cut the fish into nine, one share each, and kept nothing.
  ask : Could you have kept nothing for yourself?
  b : I'd have kept the head, I think.
  b[stage=adult|old] : I'd have been tempted. That's why it's a tale, I suppose.
  : The cat had the bones and called them the best bit. I think the cat was fibbing. Kindly.

story yg_crooked_pie [topic=memories|food]
  : Once at a feast somebody cut a pie and one piece was twice as big as all the rest.
  : Everybody looked at it. Nobody said anything. Then two folk reached for it at once.
  b : What happened then? Did they fight?
  : They didn't fight. They glared. I've cut everything even since. A crooked cut starts a quarrel.

rule @yg_even_bark
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say #exactly# the same. Look. | One more cut. Then they're even. | #saying#.

rule @yg_frost_bark
when concept=bark here.season=winter here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 12h
say All white! Nobody step on it yet. | Look at the gate. All white.

rule @yg_hungry_bark
when concept=bark self.hungry=yes
does aside
cooldown 10h
say Not yet. Wait till the lamps. | Stop it, belly. I said later.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. What do you want? If I know, I'll say. | #greet#. Be quick. I've a cut half done.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #greet#, #topic.player#. Back. I guessed you'd be. | #topic.player#. I remember you. You were polite.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : It's late. I should be indoors by now. | I'm going in soon. What is it?
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : I'll talk from here. | Not closer. Not till I know you.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=child] : Lessons. Sharing sums are my best ones. | #self.trade_words.capitalize#. I do my sums carefully. Nobody checks them twice.
dlg @2 resident.job : I help. I cut things up even. That's what I'm good at. | I'm too young for a job. I'd be good at one, though.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : Somebody at the gate said #world.news#. From #world.news_from#. That's exactly what they said. | From #world.news_from#: #world.news#. Twice I heard it, the same.
dlg @2 resident.news [world.event_words] : Everyone's on about #world.event_words#. Even the carters.
dlg @3 resident.news [!world.news !world.event_words world.wagons!=raided world.death!=recent world.wedding!=recent] : Nothing new. I listen; there's nothing. | #news_none# The carters had nothing either.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip!=yes] : I don't tell gossip. It always gets bigger. | #gossip_none#
dlg @1 resident.bye : Bye. | Bye. Go the straight way.
graft resident.hub
choice Why do you cut everything so even? -> even
node even
say Because if one piece is bigger, somebody's sad and somebody's cross. If they're all the same, nobody is. It's easy, if you're careful.
mood calm
free
choice Show me how. -> even_how
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node even_how
say You look at the whole thing first. Then you mark it. Then you cut once. If your knife's blunt, you can't. That's why I want a sharp one.
choice I'll remember that. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye


adolescent
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. I'm not little any more, so don't say it. | #greet#. Go on.
line @1 answer.how : All right. Busy. I've errands. | Even. Same as ever.
line @1 react.news.new : Who said? Exactly? | #oath#. I hadn't heard.
line @1 farewell.return : See you, then. | Bye. Mind the gate.
line @1 take_offence : I'm not a pup now. Speak to me straight. | Laugh all you like. I'm right.
rule @ad_carts_bark
when concept=bark here.time=day
does aside
cooldown 10h
say Three carts through the gate already. Two of them half empty. | That driver's counting sacks twice. Fair enough.

scene ad_errand_coin
when topic=work|day self.working=yes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I carried a parcel up from the gate and got a copper for it. Half's going home. | I'm doing errands now. Every coin I get, I split. Half home, half saved. | I've been running parcels. I'm fast because I don't take the long way.
b[stage=adult|old] #grown : Good pup. | Saving for what? | Mind you're not cheated.
b : Half? | Saved for what? | Fast?
a@grown : I'm not a pup now. I'm just fair. | A knife. A proper one. Don't laugh. | I count the coins out loud. Nobody tries it on.
a : Half. It's even. That's how I do it. | A knife. A good one. I've nearly a quarter of it. | Fast. Straight lines. No stopping to look at things.

scene ad_houses
when topic=times|lore here.region=ridgemere
does give.opinion / disagree / concede / ack
a : You can tell which Houses aren't speaking by how their carts pass at the gate. Nobody gives way. | None of the Houses would share with the others. I've watched. | Every House says the others cheat. They can't all be right. Or they can.
b : You're young to judge. | Watch all you like. | Could be.
a : I'm not judging. I'm counting. That's different. | I will. Somebody has to. | Could be. I'd rather be wrong. I'm not often, though.
b : #bc_fair# | #bc_we_will_see# | #bc_maybe#

scene ad_tales
when topic=pastimes|lore
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I still like the old tales. Nobody my age hears that from me. | I wrote down an old tale so it can't change. Word for word. | Somebody my age told an old tale wrong to sound clever. I didn't say anything. This time.
b : Nothing wrong with that. | Word for word? | This time?
a : I know. I still keep it quiet. | Every word. Small, on an old slate. | This time. Next time I might.

scene ad_frost
when topic=weather|season here.season=winter here.time=dawn
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : Another white morning. I'm too old to go and make footprints. I made them anyway. | First frost of the year. I'm always out to see it before the carts. | Mornings like this, the whole street looks new till the carts.
b : Nobody saw you. | Always? | It doesn't last.
a : Nobody saw. Straight line, though. | Always. I'll stop when I'm old. Maybe. | It doesn't. That's why I'm out early.

story ad_knife_saved [topic=memories|work]
  : I've put by for a proper knife since I can remember. Half of every coin, never more, never less.
  : There's one in a window by the gate. I visit it most days. I'm about halfway.
  ask : What would you wait years for?
  b : There was once. The getting was worth the wait.
  : That's what I'm hoping. A knife that cuts true, and never a crooked piece again.

dlg @ad resident.hub : #greet#. Ask. If I don't know, you'll hear that too.
